# `make.py --dry` builds here for checking; the published copy lives in
# pkgdown/assets/ and is the one that is committed.
TUTORIAL.html
tutorial-figures/
logo.png

# The refitted hierarchical chain, kept only so run-e.R can draw its panel
# from the same chain run-d.R summarised. Large, and regenerable.
out/hier.rds

# Freshly rendered figures. The published copies under
# pkgdown/assets/tutorial-figures/ are the committed ones, and build.py falls
# back to them, so a clean checkout can rebuild the page without re-rendering.
out/png/

# Written when a captured block fails, or when a block marked as a refusal
# does not refuse. Should never exist in a clean tree.
out/*.problem

# The skeleton preview: a review artifact for the third-pass structure, built
# by make_skeleton.py. Regenerable from content_skeleton.py, and deliberately
# not published -- the site root allowlist in tools/clean-site.R would fail the
# publish on it, which is the right answer.
preview/
